meta {
  name: 06_UnitHierarchyDelegationDirections
  seq: 6
}

docs {
  Scenario: Which side ends up with access for each delegation direction

    When a main unit delegates to a main unit, to a person and to a subunit
    And a person delegates to a main unit and to a person
    And a subunit delegates to a main unit, to a subunit and to a person
    Then the recipient side sees the delegating party
    And a delegating subunit is returned under a main unit that carries no access itself
    And instance access on a main unit is not inherited by its subunits

  The two steps where the recipient is a subunit, main unit to subunit and subunit to
  subunit, do not pass against the deployed API. A person with a key role on the main unit
  above the receiving subunit does not reach the delegating party at all, even though a
  key role on a main unit otherwise carries down to its subunits.

  Personas come from `testdata/auth-parties-testdata/<env>.js`. The delegations are part
  of the seeded environment data, so the steps read them rather than creating them.
}
